description.narrative:
Objective of the project is to improve the socio-economic situation and living conditions in BiH while the outcome is to increase employment opportunities for youth, rural women, and vulnerable groups in Bosnia and Herzegovina. More specifically estimated results are as follows: 
- 20 percent increase (2021 being the baseline) in the number of newly employed persons from the target groups (youth less than 30 years of age, rural women, and vulnerable categories of unemployed, such as long-term unemployed, persons with disability and Roma);
- 625 young people, rural women, and individuals from vulnerable categories of unemployed (long term unemployed, persons with disabilities and Roma) employed thanks to the Action;
- 1250 unemployed young people, rural women and individuals from the vulnerable categories of unemployed (long term unemployed, persons with disabilities and Roma) benefit from the implementation of these methods (new programmes and services) in local employment bureaus;
- 5 new programmes (at least one ALMP per target group) implemented;
- 800 Roma included in awareness raising in the labour market.
